#!grafli v1
# Visual explanation of the bundled grafli skill.
# Question: how does an LLM/agent use the skill to turn a natural-
# language visualization request into a clean .grafli file?

@ note title 350,-80 "How the grafli skill works" ~xxlarge

# === Pipeline (left to right) ===
@ box prompt  "User prompt"     20,80   220x80 %secondary
@ box trigger "Skill triggers?" 280,80  220x80 %accent
@ box plan    "Plan"            540,80  220x80 %accent
@ box author  "Author + verify" 800,80  220x80 %accent
@ box output  "Clean .grafli"   1060,80 220x80 %primary

@ arrow prompt  -> trigger
@ arrow trigger -> plan    "yes"
@ arrow plan    -> author
@ arrow author  -> output

# === Notes describing each step ===
@ note prompt_text 20,200 """
Visualization intent
- draw / diagram of X
- sketch / map out
- visualize this
- make a grafli
- open .grafli file
""" ~small

@ note trigger_text 280,200 """
Activates ONLY on
clear visual intent.
Plain review-code or
explain-function do
NOT trigger the skill.
Asks 1 line if unclear.
""" ~small

@ note plan_code 540,200 """
code:
plan(prompt)
question(prompt)
list_cast()
pick_flow_dir()
make_containers()
place_children()
draw_arrows()
write_notes()
re_read()
render_and_verify()
""" ~small

@ note author_code 800,200 """
code:
loop:
  write .grafli
  png = grafli render
  inspect png
  if overlap or cross:
    shorten line
    use ~small
    move box
    iterate
done
""" ~small

@ note output_text 1060,200 """
.grafli output
- plain text, diffable
- one element per line
- live-reloads in app
- versions in git
- export PNG / SVG
""" ~small
